items.spec:
Evidence: Get-PestoTicketText has no OU, DC, VerifiedBy or Reference, and dates its timeline in UTC (Workspace.ps1:202-221).
Add:
- the OU before and after as a readable path (Lyon › Postes), using the existing DN functions;
- local start and end dates;
- the controller (Plan.DC);
- VerifiedBy and VerifiedUtc, or 'Non vérifié — suivi facultatif';
- Plan.Reference;
- the next step (Get-PestoNativeGuidance).
Masked mode also masks the OU leaves, the DC and the reference. Masking stays on by default (point 59). The timeline uses local time.

Evidence: qualification.py:21 leaves every environment field at None, and :9-16 is a fixed scenario list. Test-PestoEnvironment.ps1:13 reports [Environment]::Version, which reads 4.0.30319 for every .NET 4.6+, and has no culture, DPI or domain fields.
Changes:
(1) qualification.py matrix --dimensions FILE --build SHA --output NEW. FILE holds windows, language, dotnet, account and policy lists, a mode (full or pairwise), and include/exclude lists. Case ids look like 'matrix/<w>|<l>|<d>|<a>|<p>', all NOT_RUN, each with an environment dict. Pairwise is deterministic and greedy, and covers every pair.
(2) coverage --input: counts per dimension value, the combinations never PASS, and the pairs never covered by a PASS. Support for neighbouring combinations is never inferred.
(3) attach-environment --case ID --environment env.json stores the report hash and refuses observed fields that contradict the case. Outputs use CreateNew.
(4) Test-PestoEnvironment.ps1, read-only, adds:
- DotNetRelease (HKLM NDP v4 Full Release), mapped by a pure ConvertTo-PestoDotNetVersion (528040 → 4.8, 533320 → 4.8.1, 461808 → 4.7.2…);
- ClrVersion (the old field, renamed);
- OS DisplayVersion, CurrentBuild and UBR;
- InstalledUICulture, CurrentUICulture and CurrentCulture;
- PartOfDomain and DomainRole;
- token elevation and session id;
- the high-contrast flag;
- AppliedDPI.
Keep the 'no compatibility inferred' statement.
